# critic2 EAM potential index: file name, then the elements it covers.
#
# The first entry whose elements cover every species in the system is the one
# used when no potential is named explicitly. The order is therefore the
# selection policy: for each element the community-standard potential comes
# first, then the Zhou-2004 universal set, then alloy-specific potentials,
# then the 16-metal Zhou file as a last resort for arbitrary mixtures.
# See README for provenance, citations and licence.
#
# -- element-specific potentials preferred for their element --
Cu_mishin1.eam.alloy         Cu
Fe_mm.eam.fs                 Fe
Mg_mm.eam.fs                 Mg
Zr_mm.eam.fs                 Zr
#
# -- Zhou et al. 2004 universal set, one file per element --
Al_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Al
Ag_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Ag
Au_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Au
Co_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Co
Cu_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Cu
Fe_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Fe
Mg_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Mg
Mo_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Mo
Ni_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Ni
Pb_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Pb
Pd_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Pd
Pt_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Pt
Ta_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Ta
Ti_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Ti
W_zhou2004.eam.alloy         W
Zr_zhou2004.eam.alloy        Zr
Cr_lin2008.eam.alloy         Cr
#
# -- alloy-specific potentials (also the only source here for V) --
AlCu.eam.alloy               Al Cu
CuNi.eam.alloy               Ni Cu
CoAl.eam.alloy               Co Al
CuTa.eam.alloy               Cu Ta
AlFe_mm.eam.fs               Al Fe
CuZr_mm.eam.fs               Cu Zr
VFe_mm.eam.fs                V Fe
NiAlH_jea.eam.fs             Ni Al H
NiAlH_jea.eam.alloy          Ni Al H
#
# -- last resort: every binary among the 16 Zhou metals, by mixing rule --
Zhou2004_16metals.eam.alloy  Cu Ag Au Ni Pd Pt Al Pb Fe Mo Ta W Mg Co Ti Zr
